- [Configuring hardware appliance network parameters](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/appliance-configure-network.md): Configure network parameters for your Storage Gateway Hardware Appliance.
- [Activating your hardware appliance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/appliance-activation.md): Activate your hardware appliance as a Storage Gateway.
- [Creating a gateway on your hardware appliance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/appliance-launch-gateway.md): Create a Storage Gateway on the Storage Gateway Hardware Appliance.
- [Configuring a gateway IP address on the hardware appliance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/appliance-configure-ip.md): Configure the gateway IP address on the hardware appliance to work with applications.
- [Removing gateway software from your hardware appliance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/appliance-remove-gateway.md): Remove gateway software from your Storage Gateway Hardware Appliance.
- [Deleting your hardware appliance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/delete-appliance.md): Delete your Storage Gateway Hardware Appliance from your AWS account.


## [Creating your gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/creating-your-gateway.md)

- [Creating a Volume Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/create-volume-gateway.md): Find instructions on how to download, deploy, and activate a Volume Gateway.
- [Creating a volume](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/GettingStartedCreateVolumes.md): Create volumes to store your data, now that you have activated your gateway.
- [Connecting your volumes to your client](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/GettingStartedAccessVolumes.md): Learn how to connect your gateway volumes to your client.
- [Initializing and formatting your volume](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/format-volume.md): After you use the iSCSI initiator in your client to connect to your volumes, you initialize and format your volume.
- [Testing your gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/GettingStartedTestGatewayMain.md): Test your setup on Microsoft Windows by writing data to the volume, taking a snapshot, and restoring the snapshot to another volume.
- [Backing up your volumes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/backing-up-volumes.md): Learn how to back up your Storage Gateway volumes.
- [Where do I go from here?](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/GettingStartedWhatsNextStep3.md): Find additional resources to learn more about Storage Gateway.
- [Activating your gateway in a virtual private cloud](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/gateway-private-link.md): Additional information on activating a gateway in a VPC.


## [Managing Your Volume Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/managing-gateway-common.md)

- [Editing Gateway Information](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/edit-gateway-information.md): Edit basic information for an existing Storage Gateway
- [Adding and expanding volumes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/volume-size-increase.md): Learn how to add more volumes or expand the size of existing volumes as your application needs grow.
- [Cloning a volume](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/clone-volume.md): Learn how to create a new volume from the most recent recovery point of an existing volume.
- [Viewing volume usage](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/volume-usage.md): Learn how to view the amount of data stored on a volume using the Storage Gateway console.
- [Deleting storage volumes](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/ApplicationStorageVolumesCached-Removing.md): Remove Storage Gateway cached volumes as application needs change.
- [Moving Your Volumes to a Different Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/attach-detach-volume.md): Attach and detach a volume from a gateway in Storage Gateway to move it or to refresh your underlying hardware.
- [Creating a recovery snapshot](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/snapshot.md): Learn about how to create a recovery snapshot from a volume recovery point.
- [Editing a snapshot schedule](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/SchedulingSnapshot.md): Learn how to change a snapshot schedule by specifying either the time the snapshot occurs each day or the frequency or both.
- [Deleting Snapshots](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/DeletingASnapshot.md): Learn how to delete a snapshot of your storage volume.
- [Understanding Volume Status and Transitions](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/StorageVolumeStatuses.md): Understand the possible status values for your volume and transitions between statuses as shown in the Storage Gateway console.

### [Moving your data to a new gateway instance](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/migrate-data.md)

Move data between gateway instances in Storage Gateway when you want to improve performance or to respond to a notification to migrate the gateway.

- [Moving stored volumes to a new stored Volume Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/migrate-data-volume-stored.md): Learn how to migrate your stored volumes to a new stored Volume Gateway virtual machine.
- [Moving cached volumes to a new gateway virtual machine](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/migrate-data-volume-cached.md): Learn how to migrate your cached volumes to a new cached Volume Gateway virtual machine.


## [Monitoring Storage Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/Main_monitoring-gateways-common.md)

- [Understanding gateway metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/MonitoringGateways-common.md): Learn about the metrics that help you monitor your Storage Gateway appliance.
- [Monitoring the upload buffer](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/PerfUploadBuffer-common.md): Learn how to monitor the gateway upload buffer and create an alarm for when the buffer exceeds a specified threshold.
- [Monitoring cache storage](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/PerfCache-common.md): Learn how to monitor the cache storage of a gateway in a cached volumes setup.
- [Understanding CloudWatch alarms](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/cloudwatch-alarms.md): Learn about CloudWatch alarms, which monitor information about your gateway based on metrics and expressions.
- [Creating recommended CloudWatch alarms](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/cloudwatch-alarms-create-recommended.md): Create recommended CloudWatch alarms for your gateway.
- [Creating a custom CloudWatch alarm](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/cloudwatch-alarms-create-alarm.md): Learn how to create CloudWatch alarms that send you notifications when a metric changes state.

### [Monitoring your Volume Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/monitoring-volume-gateway.md)

Monitor your gateway, volumes associated with the gateway, and the upload buffer.

- [Getting Volume Gateway health logs](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/cw-log-groups-volume.md): Learn to use Amazon CloudWatch Logs to get information about your Volume Gateway and related resources.
- [Using Amazon CloudWatch Metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/UsingCloudWatchConsole-common.md): Get monitoring data for your gateway using either the AWS Management Console or the CloudWatch API.
- [Measuring Performance Between Your Application and Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/PerfAppGateway-common.md): Measure performance of data throughput, data latency, and operations per second between your application and your gateway.
- [Measuring Performance Between Your Gateway and AWS](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/PerfGatewayAWS-common.md): Measure performance of data throughput, data latency, and operations per second between your gateway and AWS.
- [Understanding volume metrics](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/MonitoringVolumes-common.md): Learn about the Storage Gateway metrics that cover the volumes associated with your gateways.


## [Maintaining Your Gateway](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/maintaining-gateway.md)

### [Managing local disks](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/ManagingLocalStorage-common.md)

Learn how to manage and allocate the local disks that your gateway virtual machine uses for buffering and storage.

- [Deciding the amount of local disk storage](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/decide-local-disks-and-sizes.md): Learn how to properly size the local disks that your gateway uses for cache and upload buffer.
- [Add upload buffer or cache storage](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/ConfiguringLocalDiskStorage.md): Configure additional upload buffer and cache storage space for your Volume Gateway.
- [Managing Bandwidth](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/MaintenanceUpdateBandwidth-common.md): Update the bandwidth-rate limits for your gateway.

### [Managing gateway updates](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/MaintenanceManagingUpdate-common.md)

Use the Storage Gateway console to turn gateway maintenance updates updates on or off, or configure an update schedule.

- [Turn maintenance updates on or off](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/maintenance-updates-on-off.md): Use the Storage Gateway console to turn maintenance updates on or off for a specific gateway.
- [Modify the gateway maintenance window schedule](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/configure-maintenance-window-schedule.md): Use the Storage Gateway console to configure the maintenance window schedule for a specific gateway.
- [Apply an update manually](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/apply-update-manually.md): Learn how to manually apply a gateway appliance software update using the Storage Gateway console.
- [Shutting Down Your Gateway VM](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/MaintenanceShutDown-common.md): Learn how to shutdown or reboot your gateway virtual machine for maintenance, such as when applying a patch to your hypervisor.
- [Deleting your gateway and removing resources](https://docs.aws.amazon.com/storagegateway/latest/vgw/deleting-gateway-common.md): Delete your gateway using the AWS Storage Gateway console and clean up associated resources.


